{"name":"Patch of Land","hex":"#225511","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"patch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of cloth, or other suitable material, sewed or otherwise fixed upon a garment to repair or strengthen it, especially upon an old garment to cover a hole.","A small piece of anything used to repair damage or a breach; as, a patch on a kettle, a roof, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To mend by sewing on a piece or pieces of cloth, leather, or the like.","To mend with pieces; to repair by fastening pieces on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patch"},{"term":"land","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of Earth which is not covered by oceans or other bodies of water.","Real estate or landed property; a partitioned and measurable area which is owned and acquired and on which buildings and structures can be built and erected."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To descend to a surface, especially from the air.","To alight, to descend from a vehicle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/land"}],"entries":[{"title":"Patch of Land","blocks":[{"text":"Patch of Land was a peer-to-peer real estate crowdfunding online marketplace and hard money loan provider that connected real estate developers needing financing to lenders and real estate investors. Patch of Land focused on 6–24 months real-estate first lien mortgage loans with borrower guarantees."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patch_of_Land","wikidata":"Q30324595"},{"title":"Land","blocks":[{"text":"Land, also known as dry land, ground, or earth, is the solid terrestrial surface of Earth not submerged by the ocean or another body of water. It makes up approximately 29% of Earth's surface and includes all continents and islands. Earth's land surface is almost entirely covered by regolith, a layer of rock, soil, and minerals that forms the outer part of the crust. Land plays an important role in Earth's climate system, being involved in the carbon cycle, nitrogen cycle, and water cycle. One-third of land is covered in trees another third is used for agriculture, and roughly one-tenth is covered in glacier ice. The remainder consists of desert, savannah, and prairie."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Coastline_as_seen_from_Chimney_Rock%2C_Point_Reyes_National_Seashore.jpg/330px-Coastline_as_seen_from_Chimney_Rock%2C_Point_Reyes_National_Seashore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Land","wikidata":"Q11081619"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Earth_formation.jpg/500px-Earth_formation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Earth_formation.jpg/1280px-Earth_formation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Earth_formation.jpg/500px-Earth_formation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Artist's conception of Hadean Eon Earth","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarth_formation.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Continental_models.gif/500px-Continental_models.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Continental_models.gif/1280px-Continental_models.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Continental_models.gif/500px-Continental_models.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Animated map showing the world's continents according to different models","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AContinental_mode